{"duration_api_ms":261131,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"960d58aa-18ff-4924-a33a-55baf448094f","total_cost_usd":1.0377938,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72503,"cache_read_input_tokens":889,"output_tokens":20047,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":11453},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":72503,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":20047,"cache_read_input_tokens":889,"cache_creation_input_tokens":72503,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":72503},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":56584,"outputTokens":12,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.056644,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":20047,"cacheReadInputTokens":889,"cacheCreationInputTokens":72503,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9811498,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":11453,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"tool_name\":\"final\",\"paths\":[],\"final\":{\"response\":\"contract_version: 0.1.0\\nartifact_version: 1\\nwork_item: 20261007T114835\\nobservable_behaviour:\\n  - id: suite-leaves-usage-log-unchanged\\n    behaviour: \\\"Count the lines in every file under `logs/usage/`, run `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q`, then count again. The counts are the same and no new file has appeared in `logs/usage/`.\\\"\\n  - id: guard-stops-unredirected-recording\\n    behaviour: \\\"While the test suite runs, any call that would make `harness.usage.append_jsonl` write to the real usage directory is stopped before anything is written. This covers a call through `record_run` with no `log_dir`, a direct call with no `log_dir`, and a call with an explicit `log_dir` that resolves to the real directory or to a folder inside it. The calling test fails, and the failure message names the directory it tried to write to.\\\"\\n  - id: guard-demonstrated-by-purpose-written-test\\n    behaviour: \\\"A new test module, `tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py`, shows the guard stopping such a write. Its guard tests fail on the base commit 6d3dd93 with `DID NOT RAISE` and pass on the candidate.\\\"\\n  - id: recording-still-exercised\\n    behaviour: \\\"Tests that exercise usage recording still record, now into a temporary directory, and still pass. This covers `tests/unit/test_usage.py`, `test_a_budget_trip_still_records_its_usage`, and the legacy tool-loop tests that run with `record_usage=True`. The shared non-autouse `usage_log_dir` fixture in `tests/conftest.py` sends the recorder to `tmp_path / \\\\\\\"usage\\\\\\\"` and returns that path.\\\"\\n  - id: guard-not-a-blanket-block\\n    behaviour: \\\"A call that passes an explicit temporary `log_dir`, or that runs under the `usage_log_dir` fixture, writes normally. It returns a path inside the temporary directory.\\\"\\nrequired_outputs:\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/conftest.py\\n    reason: \\\"The plan's change 1: a session-scoped autouse guard around `harness.usage.append_jsonl`, plus the shared `usage_log_dir` fixture. The existing `sys.path` logic stays as it is.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py\\n    reason: \\\"The plan's change 2: the purpose-written test that request refusal items 1 and 2 call for, with positive controls.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: releases/_next/tests-never-write-usage-log.md\\n    reason: \\\"Delivery contract (`.method.yaml` delivery, `releases/README.md`, `pr-checks.yml`): every PR adds exactly one release note. It is typed patch.\\\"\\npermitted_files:\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/unit/test_agent_loop.py\\n    reason: \\\"Plan change 3: add a module-level `pytestmark = pytest.mark.usefixtures(\\\\\\\"usage_log_dir\\\\\\\")`. The `run()` helper and direct `ask` calls record by default.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/unit/test_run_cli.py\\n    reason: \\\"Plan change 4: the same module-level opt-in marker. Four `converse` tests record by default.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/unit/test_live_tier.py\\n    reason: \\\"Plan change 5: the same module-level opt-in marker. The default and end-to-end paths of `live.run_trial` record by default.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/live/test_live_eval.py\\n    reason: \\\"Plan change 6: the same module-level opt-in marker, so the manual paid tier is not stopped by the guard (see decision-live-tier-usage).\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/unit/test_demo.py\\n    reason: \\\"Contingent. Changed only if the guard shows a writer the plan did not list. The only change allowed is adding the `usage_log_dir` opt-in marker.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/unit/test_golden_cases.py\\n    reason: \\\"Contingent. Changed only if the guard shows a writer the plan did not list. The only change allowed is adding the `usage_log_dir` opt-in marker.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/unit/test_rendering.py\\n    reason: \\\"Contingent. Changed only if the guard shows a writer the plan did not list. The only change allowed is adding the `usage_log_dir` opt-in marker.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/unit/test_intent_boundary.py\\n    reason: \\\"Contingent. Changed only if the guard shows a writer the plan did not list. The only change allowed is adding the `usage_log_dir` opt-in marker.\\\"\\ndeterministic:\\n  - id: guard-module-passes\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: |-\\n      .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py -q\\n    kind: behaviour\\n    expected: \\\"Fails on the base commit because `tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py` does not exist there: pytest exits 4 with 'file or directory not found'. Passes once the guard is in `tests/conftest.py` and the module exists: every guard test and positive control passes.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_matches: '\\\\d+ passed'\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ (failed|xpassed|error)'\\n  - id: guard-test-fails-on-base-tree\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: |-\\n      bash -c 'R=\\\"$(pwd)\\\"; T=\\\"$(mktemp -d)\\\"; git archive 6d3dd93244d7bc8b87f2bb66bf2e0dd20b03b159 | tar -x -C \\\"$T\\\"; if cp tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py \\\"$T/tests/unit/\\\"; then (cd \\\"$T\\\" && \\\"$R/.venv/bin/python\\\" -m pytest tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py -q -p no:cacheprovider); echo \\\"base_exit=$?\\\"; else echo \\\"base_exit=missing-test\\\"; fi; rm -rf \\\"$T\\\"'\\n    kind: behaviour\\n    expected: \\\"Runs the candidate's guard test module against an extracted copy of the base tree. The copy's own `logs/usage/` is inside the temporary directory, so the real directory is never touched. On the base commit it fails because the test module does not exist yet: the command prints `base_exit=missing-test`. On the candidate the guard tests fail in the base copy with `DID NOT RAISE`, because base code has no guard and `record_run` swallows any `Exception`. The command then prints `base_exit=1`. This shows that the demonstration measures the change (request refusal item 2).\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_matches: 'DID NOT RAISE'\\n      stdout_excludes: 'base_exit=(0|missing-test)'\\n  - id: usage-log-unchanged-by-suite\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: |-\\n      bash -c 'snap(){ if [ -d logs/usage ]; then find logs/usage -type f -exec wc -l {} \\\\; | sort; ls -1 logs/usage; fi; }; B=\\\"$(snap)\\\"; .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q >/dev/null 2>&1; rc=$?; A=\\\"$(snap)\\\"; if [ \\\"$B\\\" = \\\"$A\\\" ]; then echo \\\"suite_exit=$rc usage_log=UNCHANGED\\\"; else echo \\\"suite_exit=$rc usage_log=CHANGED\\\"; fi'\\n    kind: behaviour\\n    expected: \\\"This is request item 1, checked against the real directory. It fails on the base commit because the legacy tool-loop tests in test_agent_loop.py, test_run_cli.py and test_live_tier.py append `function:*` records to `logs/usage/usage-<UTC date>.jsonl`, so the command prints `usage_log=CHANGED`. It passes once those tests use `usage_log_dir` and the guard stops any other writer: the suite exits 0 and the file names and line counts are identical before and after. See decision-base-dry-run-writes.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_matches: '^suite_exit=0 usage_log=UNCHANGED$'\\n  - id: release-note-present-and-shaped\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: |-\\n      .venv/bin/python -c \\\"import pathlib,re; t=pathlib.Path('releases/_next/tests-never-write-usage-log.md').read_text(); v=t.split('## Verification',1)[1].split('\\\\n## ',1)[0]; ok=all([re.search(r'(?m)^\\\\*\\\\*Type:\\\\*\\\\* *patch *$',t), re.search(r'(?m)^## Local deployment',t), re.search(r'(?m)^## Manual steps',t), re.search(r'(?m)^## Rollback',t), re.search(r'(?m)^\\\\x60{3}bash',v)]); print('NOTES_OK' if ok else 'NOTES_BAD'); raise SystemExit(0 if ok else 1)\\\"\\n    kind: behaviour\\n    expected: \\\"Fails on the base commit because `releases/_next/tests-never-write-usage-log.md` does not exist (FileNotFoundError). Passes once the note exists with a `**Type:** patch` line and the `## Local deployment`, `## Manual steps`, `## Verification` (with at least one fenced bash block) and `## Rollback` sections. The command prints NOTES_OK.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_matches: '^NOTES_OK$'\\n  - id: full-test-suite\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: |-\\n      .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\\n    kind: regression\\n    expected: \\\"The repository's declared verify command exits zero with no failures, errors or unexpected passes. The existing strict xfail (O-8) stays xfailed. Pass, skip and xfail counts equal the base counts plus the new guard tests.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ (failed|xpassed|error)'\\n  - id: recording-tests-still-pass\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: |-\\n      .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_usage.py \\\"tests/unit/test_agent_loop.py::test_a_budget_trip_still_records_its_usage\\\" -q\\n    kind: regression\\n    expected: \\\"The tests that assert usage records in a temporary directory pass before and after the change (request item 2).\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_matches: '\\\\d+ passed'\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ (failed|xpassed|error)'\\n  - id: live-tier-still-collects\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: |-\\n      .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/live --collect-only -q -m live\\n    kind: regression\\n    expected: \\\"The manual live tier still collects under `-m live`. Nothing is run and no tokens are spent.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_matches: '\\\\d+ tests? collected'\\n  - id: no-product-code-changed\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: |-\\n      git diff --quiet 6d3dd93244d7bc8b87f2bb66bf2e0dd20b03b159 -- harness config evals prompts contract server sql pytest.ini logging_config.yaml requirements.txt run.py demo.py capture.py authcheck.py VERSION .method.yaml .github .claude\\n    kind: regression\\n    expected: \\\"Exits 0: no product, configuration, evaluation, contract, entry-point, gate, VERSION or method-declaration file differs from the base commit. Exits 1 if any does.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\nmust_not_change:\\n  - invariant: \\\"`harness/usage.py`: the signatures and product behaviour of `append_jsonl` and `record_run`, including the `settings.USAGE_LOG_DIR` fallback and the rule that `record_run` never raises (ADR-005).\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"`config/settings.py`: `USAGE_LOG_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \\\\\\\"logs\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"usage\\\\\\\"`.\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"The usage record format: `LlmRequestRecord`, `RunSummaryRecord` and `SCHEMA_VERSION`.\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"What the product records in normal use, outside the test suite.\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"Existing files under `logs/usage/`. They are not deleted, truncated or edited by the executor or by any test.\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"`pytest.ini` and its `addopts = -m \\\\\\\"not live\\\\\\\"`.\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"`VERSION`. No `releases/v*.md` file is added.\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"The assertions of existing tests. No existing test is deleted, skipped, xfailed or rewritten to get around the guard. Edits to existing test modules are limited to adding the `usage_log_dir` opt-in marker.\\\"\\n  - invariant: \\\"The existing `sys.path` logic in `tests/conftest.py`.\\\"\\nfailure_behaviour:\\n  - condition: \\\"A test calls `usage.record_run(...)` with no `log_dir`, and `settings.USAGE_LOG_DIR` still points at the real `logs/usage/`.\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The guard calls `pytest.fail` before anything is written. `Failed` is a `BaseException`, so it passes through `record_run`'s `except Exception`. The test is reported as failed, not as an error, and the failure is not swallowed. The message names the resolved target directory and the protected directory, cites ADR-021, and names the fix: use the `usage_log_dir` fixture or pass `log_dir=tmp_path`. No file under `logs/usage/` is created or grows.\\\"\\n  - condition: \\\"A test calls `usage.append_jsonl(...)` directly with no `log_dir` while the real directory is in effect.\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The same failure, raised before the directory is created or a file is opened.\\\"\\n  - condition: \\\"A test passes an explicit `log_dir` that resolves to the real directory or to a folder inside it, such as `REAL / \\\\\\\"x\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"..\\\\\\\"` or a subdirectory.\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The same failure. The target is resolved before it is compared with the protected directories.\\\"\\n  - condition: \\\"A test monkeypatches `settings.USAGE_LOG_DIR` back to the real directory.\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"It is still stopped. The protected directories were captured when `tests/conftest.py` was imported, before any test ran, and the target is read from `settings` at call time.\\\"\\n  - condition: \\\"A legacy tool-loop run goes through `ask`/`converse`/`live.run_trial` with `record_usage=True` in a module that has not opted into `usage_log_dir`.\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The test fails and names the real directory. The fix is to add the opt-in marker to that module, inside the permitted files. The guard is never weakened.\\\"\\nfailure_behaviour_note_placeholder: null\\ncompatibility:\\n  - obligation: \\\"ADR-021: 'Tests never write to `logs/usage/`.' This contract enforces only this sentence. The pipeline request and run-summary records are not part of it.\\\"\\n  - obligation: \\\"ADR-005: `record_run()` never raises in product use. The guard exists only inside the test session (`tests/conftest.py`), and product code is unchanged.\\\"\\n  - obligation: \\\"ADR-007: the live tier stays manual and excluded by default (`-m \\\\\\\"not live\\\\\\\"`), never a PR gate.\\\"\\n  - obligation: \\\"Delivery contract: exactly one `releases/_next/*.md` is added, `VERSION` is untouched, and the note is typed patch because only `tests/**` and `releases/**` change (`.method.yaml` release classes).\\\"\\n  - obligation: \\\"The supported interpreters are CPython 3.10 to 3.13 (`pr-checks.yml` uses 3.12). `Path.is_relative_to` is available on all of them.\\\"\\ncompatibility_baselines: []\\ncontract_requirements:\\n  - id: scope-is-the-file-list\\n    requirement: \\\"The permitted change set is exactly `required_outputs` plus `permitted_files` in k-12Harness. The work-store is never written by the executor. A change to the contingent test modules is allowed only when the guard shows that module writing to the real directory, and the change is limited to adding the `usage_log_dir` opt-in marker.\\\"\\n  - id: guard-mechanism\\n    requirement: \\\"The guard wraps `harness.usage.append_jsonl` for the whole session, with the same signature, and fails through `pytest.fail` before any write. It does not use a teardown check, a silent redirect on its own, or a session-wide directory snapshot (plan, rejected alternatives).\\\"\\n  - id: decision-base-dry-run-writes\\n    requirement: \\\"DECISION: may the controller's dry run against base commit 6d3dd93 execute the base test suite in place? The base code has no guard, so `full-test-suite` and `usage-log-unchanged-by-suite`, run on base, append scripted-model records to the real `logs/usage/`. The plan avoided exactly that for its own base check. Options: (a) accept it: the directory is untracked, already contaminated, and cleaning it is out of scope; the contract stands as written. (b) no base run may write there: both criteria run only on the candidate, and a human records the base result as accepted; or they are rewritten to run the suite in an isolated copy of the tree (as `guard-test-fails-on-base-tree` does), with the base failure shown by a copy-based count of the copy's own `logs/usage/`. Affects: deterministic `full-test-suite` and `usage-log-unchanged-by-suite`, and observable_behaviour suite-leaves-usage-log-unchanged. This contract is written on option (a), because the repository's declared verify command must be run and the plan's verification step 2 runs the suite in place.\\\"\\n  - id: decision-live-tier-usage\\n    requirement: \\\"DECISION: should paid live-tier runs (`tests/live/test_live_eval.py`, run by hand with `-m live`) still record usage in the real `logs/usage/`? Options: (a) no: follow ADR-021 literally and redirect the module with `usage_log_dir` (the plan's choice); real-model live-test telemetry then no longer lands in `logs/usage/`. (b) yes: exempt live-marked tests from the guard, which needs an exemption rule in `tests/conftest.py`, leaves `tests/live/test_live_eval.py` unchanged, and departs from ADR-021's wording. Affects: permitted_files `tests/live/test_live_eval.py`, required_outputs `tests/conftest.py` (exemption logic), compatibility ADR-021, and semantic `live-tier-consistent`. This contract is written on option (a).\\\"\\n  - id: assumption-baseexception-passes\\n    requirement: \\\"ASSUMPTION: no layer between `append_jsonl` and the test catches `BaseException` (`harness/agent.py`, `evals/live.py`, `demo.py`, `run.py`, asyncio). If one does, the snapshot assertion in the demonstration test and `usage-log-unchanged-by-suite` still show it.\\\"\\n  - id: assumption-single-writer\\n    requirement: \\\"ASSUMPTION: every write to `logs/usage/` goes through `harness.usage.append_jsonl`, as it does at the base commit. A writer that bypasses it is caught only by `usage-log-unchanged-by-suite`.\\\"\\n  - id: gap-writers-inferred\\n    requirement: \\\"GAP: the plan's list of writing tests is inferred from reading the code. The guard is the authoritative detector. Writers it finds are fixed by opt-in inside the permitted files. If one turns up outside them, that is recorded as a scope defect.\\\"\\n  - id: gap-polluted-files\\n    requirement: \\\"GAP: the files already contaminated in `logs/usage/` stay in place and still distort usage reports. Cleaning them needs a separate decision.\\\"\\nsemantic:\\n  - id: guard-fails-before-write\\n    criterion: \\\"The guard decides and calls `pytest.fail` inside the wrapper, before calling the original `append_jsonl`. So the directory is not created and no file is opened for a protected target, and the outcome is a test failure, not a teardown error.\\\"\\n  - id: message-names-directory\\n    criterion: \\\"The failure message contains the resolved path the call tried to write to and the protected directory, cites ADR-021, and names the `usage_log_dir` fixture or `log_dir=tmp_path` as the fix. The demonstration test asserts that the real directory's path appears in the exception text.\\\"\\n  - id: demonstration-is-load-bearing\\n    criterion: \\\"`tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py` calls `record_run` with a real run result and no `log_dir`, and also calls `append_jsonl` directly. It asserts the failure with `pytest.raises(pytest.fail.Exception)` and asserts that a read-only snapshot of the real directory is unchanged. It would fail if the guard were removed; `guard-test-fails-on-base-tree` shows this. The test never writes to the real directory, even when it fails.\\\"\\n  - id: protected-dirs-captured-early\\n    criterion: \\\"The protected directories are captured when `tests/conftest.py` is imported. They are `settings.USAGE_LOG_DIR.resolve()` and a separately computed `(PROJECT_ROOT / \\\\\\\"logs\\\\\\\" / \\\\\\\"usage\\\\\\\").resolve()`, so a test's monkeypatch cannot move them. The target is resolved at call time from `log_dir` or the current `settings.USAGE_LOG_DIR`.\\\"\\n  - id: positive-controls-present\\n    criterion: \\\"The guard module includes positive controls. An explicit `log_dir=tmp_path` writes and returns a path under `tmp_path`, and under `usage_log_dir` a `record_run` with no `log_dir` writes into the fixture's directory. So the guard is shown not to be a blanket block.\\\"\\n  - id: opt-ins-preserve-coverage\\n    criterion: \\\"Each opt-in is a module-level `pytest.mark.usefixtures(\\\\\\\"usage_log_dir\\\\\\\")`, or the fixture itself. Recording is still exercised: no test switches to `record_usage=False`, and no test is skipped, removed or loosened to avoid the guard.\\\"\\n  - id: live-tier-consistent\\n    criterion: \\\"Under decision-live-tier-usage option (a), `tests/live/test_live_eval.py` opts into `usage_log_dir`, so a manual paid run is not stopped by the guard and does not write to the real directory.\\\"\\n  - id: release-note-accurate\\n    criterion: \\\"The release note states that only tests and release notes changed, says 'Nothing to do.' for local deployment and manual steps, and gives a pasteable Verification bash block (no comment lines) that compares the line counts in `logs/usage/` before and after the suite, with its expected output stated in prose.\\\"\\nout_of_scope:\\n  - item: \\\"Deleting, cleaning or rewriting the files already in `logs/usage/`.\\\"\\n  - item: \\\"Whether tests write to `logs/harness.log`.\\\"\\n  - item: \\\"ADR-021's pipeline request and run-summary records, the `schema_version` bump, and any change to what the product records in normal use.\\\"\\n  - item: \\\"Any change to `harness/usage.py`, `config/settings.py` or the usage record format.\\\"\\n  - item: \\\"Running the paid live tier (`tests/live` under `-m live`) as part of verification.\\\"\\n  - item: \\\"Opting pipeline-only test modules into `usage_log_dir` ahead of the future ADR-021 pipeline-recording work, unless the guard shows them writing today.\\\"\\n\"}}","structured_output":{"tool_name":"final","paths":[],"final":{"response":"contract_version: 0.1.0\nartifact_version: 1\nwork_item: 20261007T114835\nobservable_behaviour:\n  - id: suite-leaves-usage-log-unchanged\n    behaviour: \"Count the lines in every file under `logs/usage/`, run `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q`, then count again. The counts are the same and no new file has appeared in `logs/usage/`.\"\n  - id: guard-stops-unredirected-recording\n    behaviour: \"While the test suite runs, any call that would make `harness.usage.append_jsonl` write to the real usage directory is stopped before anything is written. This covers a call through `record_run` with no `log_dir`, a direct call with no `log_dir`, and a call with an explicit `log_dir` that resolves to the real directory or to a folder inside it. The calling test fails, and the failure message names the directory it tried to write to.\"\n  - id: guard-demonstrated-by-purpose-written-test\n    behaviour: \"A new test module, `tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py`, shows the guard stopping such a write. Its guard tests fail on the base commit 6d3dd93 with `DID NOT RAISE` and pass on the candidate.\"\n  - id: recording-still-exercised\n    behaviour: \"Tests that exercise usage recording still record, now into a temporary directory, and still pass. This covers `tests/unit/test_usage.py`, `test_a_budget_trip_still_records_its_usage`, and the legacy tool-loop tests that run with `record_usage=True`. The shared non-autouse `usage_log_dir` fixture in `tests/conftest.py` sends the recorder to `tmp_path / \\\"usage\\\"` and returns that path.\"\n  - id: guard-not-a-blanket-block\n    behaviour: \"A call that passes an explicit temporary `log_dir`, or that runs under the `usage_log_dir` fixture, writes normally. It returns a path inside the temporary directory.\"\nrequired_outputs:\n  - repo: k-12Harness\n    path: tests/conftest.py\n    reason: \"The plan's change 1: a session-scoped autouse guard around `harness.usage.append_jsonl`, plus the shared `usage_log_dir` fixture. The existing `sys.path` logic stays as it is.\"\n  - repo: k-12Harness\n    path: tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py\n    reason: \"The plan's change 2: the purpose-written test that request refusal items 1 and 2 call for, with positive controls.\"\n  - repo: k-12Harness\n    path: releases/_next/tests-never-write-usage-log.md\n    reason: \"Delivery contract (`.method.yaml` delivery, `releases/README.md`, `pr-checks.yml`): every PR adds exactly one release note. It is typed patch.\"\npermitted_files:\n  - repo: k-12Harness\n    path: tests/unit/test_agent_loop.py\n    reason: \"Plan change 3: add a module-level `pytestmark = pytest.mark.usefixtures(\\\"usage_log_dir\\\")`. The `run()` helper and direct `ask` calls record by default.\"\n  - repo: k-12Harness\n    path: tests/unit/test_run_cli.py\n    reason: \"Plan change 4: the same module-level opt-in marker. Four `converse` tests record by default.\"\n  - repo: k-12Harness\n    path: tests/unit/test_live_tier.py\n    reason: \"Plan change 5: the same module-level opt-in marker. The default and end-to-end paths of `live.run_trial` record by default.\"\n  - repo: k-12Harness\n    path: tests/live/test_live_eval.py\n    reason: \"Plan change 6: the same module-level opt-in marker, so the manual paid tier is not stopped by the guard (see decision-live-tier-usage).\"\n  - repo: k-12Harness\n    path: tests/unit/test_demo.py\n    reason: \"Contingent. Changed only if the guard shows a writer the plan did not list. The only change allowed is adding the `usage_log_dir` opt-in marker.\"\n  - repo: k-12Harness\n    path: tests/unit/test_golden_cases.py\n    reason: \"Contingent. Changed only if the guard shows a writer the plan did not list. The only change allowed is adding the `usage_log_dir` opt-in marker.\"\n  - repo: k-12Harness\n    path: tests/unit/test_rendering.py\n    reason: \"Contingent. Changed only if the guard shows a writer the plan did not list. The only change allowed is adding the `usage_log_dir` opt-in marker.\"\n  - repo: k-12Harness\n    path: tests/unit/test_intent_boundary.py\n    reason: \"Contingent. Changed only if the guard shows a writer the plan did not list. The only change allowed is adding the `usage_log_dir` opt-in marker.\"\ndeterministic:\n  - id: guard-module-passes\n    repo: k-12Harness\n    command: |-\n      .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py -q\n    kind: behaviour\n    expected: \"Fails on the base commit because `tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py` does not exist there: pytest exits 4 with 'file or directory not found'. Passes once the guard is in `tests/conftest.py` and the module exists: every guard test and positive control passes.\"\n    expect:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_matches: '\\d+ passed'\n      stdout_excludes: '\\d+ (failed|xpassed|error)'\n  - id: guard-test-fails-on-base-tree\n    repo: k-12Harness\n    command: |-\n      bash -c 'R=\"$(pwd)\"; T=\"$(mktemp -d)\"; git archive 6d3dd93244d7bc8b87f2bb66bf2e0dd20b03b159 | tar -x -C \"$T\"; if cp tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py \"$T/tests/unit/\"; then (cd \"$T\" && \"$R/.venv/bin/python\" -m pytest tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py -q -p no:cacheprovider); echo \"base_exit=$?\"; else echo \"base_exit=missing-test\"; fi; rm -rf \"$T\"'\n    kind: behaviour\n    expected: \"Runs the candidate's guard test module against an extracted copy of the base tree. The copy's own `logs/usage/` is inside the temporary directory, so the real directory is never touched. On the base commit it fails because the test module does not exist yet: the command prints `base_exit=missing-test`. On the candidate the guard tests fail in the base copy with `DID NOT RAISE`, because base code has no guard and `record_run` swallows any `Exception`. The command then prints `base_exit=1`. This shows that the demonstration measures the change (request refusal item 2).\"\n    expect:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_matches: 'DID NOT RAISE'\n      stdout_excludes: 'base_exit=(0|missing-test)'\n  - id: usage-log-unchanged-by-suite\n    repo: k-12Harness\n    command: |-\n      bash -c 'snap(){ if [ -d logs/usage ]; then find logs/usage -type f -exec wc -l {} \\; | sort; ls -1 logs/usage; fi; }; B=\"$(snap)\"; .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q >/dev/null 2>&1; rc=$?; A=\"$(snap)\"; if [ \"$B\" = \"$A\" ]; then echo \"suite_exit=$rc usage_log=UNCHANGED\"; else echo \"suite_exit=$rc usage_log=CHANGED\"; fi'\n    kind: behaviour\n    expected: \"This is request item 1, checked against the real directory. It fails on the base commit because the legacy tool-loop tests in test_agent_loop.py, test_run_cli.py and test_live_tier.py append `function:*` records to `logs/usage/usage-<UTC date>.jsonl`, so the command prints `usage_log=CHANGED`. It passes once those tests use `usage_log_dir` and the guard stops any other writer: the suite exits 0 and the file names and line counts are identical before and after. See decision-base-dry-run-writes.\"\n    expect:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_matches: '^suite_exit=0 usage_log=UNCHANGED$'\n  - id: release-note-present-and-shaped\n    repo: k-12Harness\n    command: |-\n      .venv/bin/python -c \"import pathlib,re; t=pathlib.Path('releases/_next/tests-never-write-usage-log.md').read_text(); v=t.split('## Verification',1)[1].split('\\n## ',1)[0]; ok=all([re.search(r'(?m)^\\*\\*Type:\\*\\* *patch *$',t), re.search(r'(?m)^## Local deployment',t), re.search(r'(?m)^## Manual steps',t), re.search(r'(?m)^## Rollback',t), re.search(r'(?m)^\\x60{3}bash',v)]); print('NOTES_OK' if ok else 'NOTES_BAD'); raise SystemExit(0 if ok else 1)\"\n    kind: behaviour\n    expected: \"Fails on the base commit because `releases/_next/tests-never-write-usage-log.md` does not exist (FileNotFoundError). Passes once the note exists with a `**Type:** patch` line and the `## Local deployment`, `## Manual steps`, `## Verification` (with at least one fenced bash block) and `## Rollback` sections. The command prints NOTES_OK.\"\n    expect:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_matches: '^NOTES_OK$'\n  - id: full-test-suite\n    repo: k-12Harness\n    command: |-\n      .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\n    kind: regression\n    expected: \"The repository's declared verify command exits zero with no failures, errors or unexpected passes. The existing strict xfail (O-8) stays xfailed. Pass, skip and xfail counts equal the base counts plus the new guard tests.\"\n    expect:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_excludes: '\\d+ (failed|xpassed|error)'\n  - id: recording-tests-still-pass\n    repo: k-12Harness\n    command: |-\n      .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_usage.py \"tests/unit/test_agent_loop.py::test_a_budget_trip_still_records_its_usage\" -q\n    kind: regression\n    expected: \"The tests that assert usage records in a temporary directory pass before and after the change (request item 2).\"\n    expect:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_matches: '\\d+ passed'\n      stdout_excludes: '\\d+ (failed|xpassed|error)'\n  - id: live-tier-still-collects\n    repo: k-12Harness\n    command: |-\n      .venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/live --collect-only -q -m live\n    kind: regression\n    expected: \"The manual live tier still collects under `-m live`. Nothing is run and no tokens are spent.\"\n    expect:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_matches: '\\d+ tests? collected'\n  - id: no-product-code-changed\n    repo: k-12Harness\n    command: |-\n      git diff --quiet 6d3dd93244d7bc8b87f2bb66bf2e0dd20b03b159 -- harness config evals prompts contract server sql pytest.ini logging_config.yaml requirements.txt run.py demo.py capture.py authcheck.py VERSION .method.yaml .github .claude\n    kind: regression\n    expected: \"Exits 0: no product, configuration, evaluation, contract, entry-point, gate, VERSION or method-declaration file differs from the base commit. Exits 1 if any does.\"\n    expect:\n      exit_code: 0\nmust_not_change:\n  - invariant: \"`harness/usage.py`: the signatures and product behaviour of `append_jsonl` and `record_run`, including the `settings.USAGE_LOG_DIR` fallback and the rule that `record_run` never raises (ADR-005).\"\n  - invariant: \"`config/settings.py`: `USAGE_LOG_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \\\"logs\\\" / \\\"usage\\\"`.\"\n  - invariant: \"The usage record format: `LlmRequestRecord`, `RunSummaryRecord` and `SCHEMA_VERSION`.\"\n  - invariant: \"What the product records in normal use, outside the test suite.\"\n  - invariant: \"Existing files under `logs/usage/`. They are not deleted, truncated or edited by the executor or by any test.\"\n  - invariant: \"`pytest.ini` and its `addopts = -m \\\"not live\\\"`.\"\n  - invariant: \"`VERSION`. No `releases/v*.md` file is added.\"\n  - invariant: \"The assertions of existing tests. No existing test is deleted, skipped, xfailed or rewritten to get around the guard. Edits to existing test modules are limited to adding the `usage_log_dir` opt-in marker.\"\n  - invariant: \"The existing `sys.path` logic in `tests/conftest.py`.\"\nfailure_behaviour:\n  - condition: \"A test calls `usage.record_run(...)` with no `log_dir`, and `settings.USAGE_LOG_DIR` still points at the real `logs/usage/`.\"\n    expected: \"The guard calls `pytest.fail` before anything is written. `Failed` is a `BaseException`, so it passes through `record_run`'s `except Exception`. The test is reported as failed, not as an error, and the failure is not swallowed. The message names the resolved target directory and the protected directory, cites ADR-021, and names the fix: use the `usage_log_dir` fixture or pass `log_dir=tmp_path`. No file under `logs/usage/` is created or grows.\"\n  - condition: \"A test calls `usage.append_jsonl(...)` directly with no `log_dir` while the real directory is in effect.\"\n    expected: \"The same failure, raised before the directory is created or a file is opened.\"\n  - condition: \"A test passes an explicit `log_dir` that resolves to the real directory or to a folder inside it, such as `REAL / \\\"x\\\" / \\\"..\\\"` or a subdirectory.\"\n    expected: \"The same failure. The target is resolved before it is compared with the protected directories.\"\n  - condition: \"A test monkeypatches `settings.USAGE_LOG_DIR` back to the real directory.\"\n    expected: \"It is still stopped. The protected directories were captured when `tests/conftest.py` was imported, before any test ran, and the target is read from `settings` at call time.\"\n  - condition: \"A legacy tool-loop run goes through `ask`/`converse`/`live.run_trial` with `record_usage=True` in a module that has not opted into `usage_log_dir`.\"\n    expected: \"The test fails and names the real directory. The fix is to add the opt-in marker to that module, inside the permitted files. The guard is never weakened.\"\nfailure_behaviour_note_placeholder: null\ncompatibility:\n  - obligation: \"ADR-021: 'Tests never write to `logs/usage/`.' This contract enforces only this sentence. The pipeline request and run-summary records are not part of it.\"\n  - obligation: \"ADR-005: `record_run()` never raises in product use. The guard exists only inside the test session (`tests/conftest.py`), and product code is unchanged.\"\n  - obligation: \"ADR-007: the live tier stays manual and excluded by default (`-m \\\"not live\\\"`), never a PR gate.\"\n  - obligation: \"Delivery contract: exactly one `releases/_next/*.md` is added, `VERSION` is untouched, and the note is typed patch because only `tests/**` and `releases/**` change (`.method.yaml` release classes).\"\n  - obligation: \"The supported interpreters are CPython 3.10 to 3.13 (`pr-checks.yml` uses 3.12). `Path.is_relative_to` is available on all of them.\"\ncompatibility_baselines: []\ncontract_requirements:\n  - id: scope-is-the-file-list\n    requirement: \"The permitted change set is exactly `required_outputs` plus `permitted_files` in k-12Harness. The work-store is never written by the executor. A change to the contingent test modules is allowed only when the guard shows that module writing to the real directory, and the change is limited to adding the `usage_log_dir` opt-in marker.\"\n  - id: guard-mechanism\n    requirement: \"The guard wraps `harness.usage.append_jsonl` for the whole session, with the same signature, and fails through `pytest.fail` before any write. It does not use a teardown check, a silent redirect on its own, or a session-wide directory snapshot (plan, rejected alternatives).\"\n  - id: decision-base-dry-run-writes\n    requirement: \"DECISION: may the controller's dry run against base commit 6d3dd93 execute the base test suite in place? The base code has no guard, so `full-test-suite` and `usage-log-unchanged-by-suite`, run on base, append scripted-model records to the real `logs/usage/`. The plan avoided exactly that for its own base check. Options: (a) accept it: the directory is untracked, already contaminated, and cleaning it is out of scope; the contract stands as written. (b) no base run may write there: both criteria run only on the candidate, and a human records the base result as accepted; or they are rewritten to run the suite in an isolated copy of the tree (as `guard-test-fails-on-base-tree` does), with the base failure shown by a copy-based count of the copy's own `logs/usage/`. Affects: deterministic `full-test-suite` and `usage-log-unchanged-by-suite`, and observable_behaviour suite-leaves-usage-log-unchanged. This contract is written on option (a), because the repository's declared verify command must be run and the plan's verification step 2 runs the suite in place.\"\n  - id: decision-live-tier-usage\n    requirement: \"DECISION: should paid live-tier runs (`tests/live/test_live_eval.py`, run by hand with `-m live`) still record usage in the real `logs/usage/`? Options: (a) no: follow ADR-021 literally and redirect the module with `usage_log_dir` (the plan's choice); real-model live-test telemetry then no longer lands in `logs/usage/`. (b) yes: exempt live-marked tests from the guard, which needs an exemption rule in `tests/conftest.py`, leaves `tests/live/test_live_eval.py` unchanged, and departs from ADR-021's wording. Affects: permitted_files `tests/live/test_live_eval.py`, required_outputs `tests/conftest.py` (exemption logic), compatibility ADR-021, and semantic `live-tier-consistent`. This contract is written on option (a).\"\n  - id: assumption-baseexception-passes\n    requirement: \"ASSUMPTION: no layer between `append_jsonl` and the test catches `BaseException` (`harness/agent.py`, `evals/live.py`, `demo.py`, `run.py`, asyncio). If one does, the snapshot assertion in the demonstration test and `usage-log-unchanged-by-suite` still show it.\"\n  - id: assumption-single-writer\n    requirement: \"ASSUMPTION: every write to `logs/usage/` goes through `harness.usage.append_jsonl`, as it does at the base commit. A writer that bypasses it is caught only by `usage-log-unchanged-by-suite`.\"\n  - id: gap-writers-inferred\n    requirement: \"GAP: the plan's list of writing tests is inferred from reading the code. The guard is the authoritative detector. Writers it finds are fixed by opt-in inside the permitted files. If one turns up outside them, that is recorded as a scope defect.\"\n  - id: gap-polluted-files\n    requirement: \"GAP: the files already contaminated in `logs/usage/` stay in place and still distort usage reports. Cleaning them needs a separate decision.\"\nsemantic:\n  - id: guard-fails-before-write\n    criterion: \"The guard decides and calls `pytest.fail` inside the wrapper, before calling the original `append_jsonl`. So the directory is not created and no file is opened for a protected target, and the outcome is a test failure, not a teardown error.\"\n  - id: message-names-directory\n    criterion: \"The failure message contains the resolved path the call tried to write to and the protected directory, cites ADR-021, and names the `usage_log_dir` fixture or `log_dir=tmp_path` as the fix. The demonstration test asserts that the real directory's path appears in the exception text.\"\n  - id: demonstration-is-load-bearing\n    criterion: \"`tests/unit/test_usage_log_guard.py` calls `record_run` with a real run result and no `log_dir`, and also calls `append_jsonl` directly. It asserts the failure with `pytest.raises(pytest.fail.Exception)` and asserts that a read-only snapshot of the real directory is unchanged. It would fail if the guard were removed; `guard-test-fails-on-base-tree` shows this. The test never writes to the real directory, even when it fails.\"\n  - id: protected-dirs-captured-early\n    criterion: \"The protected directories are captured when `tests/conftest.py` is imported. They are `settings.USAGE_LOG_DIR.resolve()` and a separately computed `(PROJECT_ROOT / \\\"logs\\\" / \\\"usage\\\").resolve()`, so a test's monkeypatch cannot move them. The target is resolved at call time from `log_dir` or the current `settings.USAGE_LOG_DIR`.\"\n  - id: positive-controls-present\n    criterion: \"The guard module includes positive controls. An explicit `log_dir=tmp_path` writes and returns a path under `tmp_path`, and under `usage_log_dir` a `record_run` with no `log_dir` writes into the fixture's directory. So the guard is shown not to be a blanket block.\"\n  - id: opt-ins-preserve-coverage\n    criterion: \"Each opt-in is a module-level `pytest.mark.usefixtures(\\\"usage_log_dir\\\")`, or the fixture itself. Recording is still exercised: no test switches to `record_usage=False`, and no test is skipped, removed or loosened to avoid the guard.\"\n  - id: live-tier-consistent\n    criterion: \"Under decision-live-tier-usage option (a), `tests/live/test_live_eval.py` opts into `usage_log_dir`, so a manual paid run is not stopped by the guard and does not write to the real directory.\"\n  - id: release-note-accurate\n    criterion: \"The release note states that only tests and release notes changed, says 'Nothing to do.' for local deployment and manual steps, and gives a pasteable Verification bash block (no comment lines) that compares the line counts in `logs/usage/` before and after the suite, with its expected output stated in prose.\"\nout_of_scope:\n  - item: \"Deleting, cleaning or rewriting the files already in `logs/usage/`.\"\n  - item: \"Whether tests write to `logs/harness.log`.\"\n  - item: \"ADR-021's pipeline request and run-summary records, the `schema_version` bump, and any change to what the product records in normal use.\"\n  - item: \"Any change to `harness/usage.py`, `config/settings.py` or the usage record format.\"\n  - item: \"Running the paid live tier (`tests/live` under `-m live`) as part of verification.\"\n  - item: \"Opting pipeline-only test modules into `usage_log_dir` ahead of the future ADR-021 pipeline-recording work, unless the guard shows them writing today.\"\n"}},"ttft_ms":167405,"type":"result","duration_ms":260225,"uuid":"7c669987-e7ed-45eb-a940-2bc0625c8672","ttft_stream_ms":3843,"time_to_request_ms":387,"first_content_frame_ms":3844,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
